From bad2d1ed664e89b5ddc501a1393e1b22a45f4687 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aravind Vijayakumar <aprasann@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:40:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] kiumd: align drivers with linux 6_18 (rebased onto 0001,
 LY030 base)

qcom_sg_ops's dma_heap_attachment stored a separately
allocated struct sg_table *, which corrupted reads of the
same struct once kiumd switched to an embedded-sg_table layout,
breaking GMU/KGSL-secure buffer maps. Embed the sg_table directly to
match, and adjust dup_sg_table()/detach/map/sync call sites accordingly.
add ctrl-pending fixed-IOVA staging for GMU/KGSL dmabuf and
mmio maps (priv and non-priv), fix missing smmu_table registration/
unmap pairing, report the real mapped IOVA to userspace, convert the
map/unmap debug printk()s to tracepoints, and add a resetting_domain
field for in-progress group device resets.

Signed-off-by: Aravind Vijayakumar <aprasann@qti.qualcomm.com>
